{
  "_comment": "Write-through cache (docs/design/write-through-cache.md). Both platforms' tests read this. Times are epoch seconds; 'now' is the time of the step. A cover version is the book's updatedAt as the server lists it. Cover files: ok | missing | empty | corrupt. A disk entry may carry the etag stored with it; a listed book may carry server_etag (the thumbnail's current ETag). download = covers whose body was transferred (200); not_modified = conditional requests answered 304 (file kept, renamed to the listed version); conditional = requests sent with If-None-Match. writes: effect is what the plugin sends the companion (Cache.writeEffect: the book id, the fields it sets, a null field is cleared, and whether Home goes stale; null when the write failed, so nothing is sent); the companion applies it to every cached reply (CacheStore.patched).",
